  "Normalized cyclic convolution over the polynomial ring $\\mathbb C[y]/(y^r+1)$ on $d-1$ axes of power-of-two length is computed with the fast tape procedures at cost $O(Tp[dK+pK^{\\tau-1}+\\ell d^{\\lambda'}+\\log(rp)])$ and error $\\sqrt2\\,M(3\\ell+1)2^{-p}$.",
  "Compute two forward synthetic transforms that keep the same frequency order, multiply the entries pointwise by signed packing, and apply the opposite transform; place the data by chunk interchanges and run each round as a simultaneous butterfly layer.",
  M("The fast layers and chunk interchanges only help if the whole convolution is organized as transforms on power-of-two axes whose cost is dominated by butterfly layers and address movement.", "reconstructed"),
  [S21, S22, S23, S24],
